From fd537a767494acf2019b3682fe366ac682a47852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AthenaBoard <dev@athenaboard.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:43:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebrand to grades 5-9 US curriculum focus; add acquisition
 pages, verifiable testimonials, and simplify board UI

Positioning
- Lead with one statement: the AI whiteboard that turns a teacher's
  explanation into a live simulation.
- Narrow to grades 5-9 Math, Science, Geography, History; surface Common
  Core / NGSS alignment throughout.
- Demote the kitchen-sink feature list to a small essentials strip.

Acquisition
- 8 Chalkie-style concept pages at clean slugs, generated from one data
  file (scripts/build-lesson-pages.js). Each has a live demo, a 45-min
  teaching outline, the standard, a disclosed teacher quote, and a CTA.
- Dynamic robots.txt + sitemap.xml driven by the same slug list.

Testimonials
- Named, role/state-attributed, verified-educator badge, and an explicit
  'received free beta access' disclosure per FTC guidance.

Interactive graph widget
- New dependency-free graphdemo.js so visitors can drag a/b/c on the
  quadratic page before signing up. No eval; families defined in code.

Whiteboard UI
- Toolbar: 5 essential tools up front, 5 advanced behind a More reveal;
  Page section collapsed by default; flowchart mode auto-reveals
  move/connect.
- Toolbar 190->160px, info panel 340->312px for more canvas.
- Fix: the More toggle shares .tool-btn styling but has no data-tool, so
  the tool click handler now ignores buttons without one.

Tests: 86 checks across graph math, board structure, and a live smoke
test of every acquisition route.
